# Responsive design — MANDATORY (PC + mobile)

**NON-NEGOTIABLE.** Do not mark UI, layout, CSS, or component work complete until both **desktop (≥1024px)** and **mobile (~375px)** are addressed in the **same change**. Never defer mobile styles to a follow-up.

This rule applies to **every** task that touches UI — features, bugfixes, refactors, new buttons, modals, lists, forms, or AI panels.

---

## Required before you finish (check every item)

Copy this checklist mentally for each change; if any item fails, fix it before responding “done”:

- [ ] **Layout** — Tested narrow (~375px) and wide (≥1024px). Flex/grid uses `min-width: 0` / `min-height: 0` where content scrolls. No overlap with fixed bottom nav or headers.
- [ ] **Touch** — Every button, chip, link, and tappable row is **≥44×44px** on mobile (`min-height` / `min-width` or padding). Add `touch-action: manipulation` on interactive controls.
- [ ] **Safe areas** — Bottom bars, modals, inputs, and pinned footers use `env(safe-area-inset-bottom)` (and top inset when full-screen). Page containers account for bottom nav padding.
- [ ] **Scroll** — Long lists and chip rows scroll in the correct container. Chip rows on small screens: horizontal scroll + `-webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch`.
- [ ] **Text** — No unreadable tiny type on mobile (avoid &lt;0.75rem for body). Long labels, verse refs, and errors use `max-width: 100%`, `overflow-wrap: break-word`.
- [ ] **Navigation** — Modals and overlays integrate with the app back-button handler on Android where applicable.
- [ ] **CSS co-located** — Mobile rules live in the **same** component CSS file (`Component.css`), inside `@media (max-width: 768px)` (use `600px` only when tighter layout is needed).

---

## Implementation rules (this project)

| Area | Requirement |
|------|-------------|
| Breakpoint | `@media (max-width: 768px)` — default mobile block for every new UI section |
| New buttons/chips | Add base + mobile styles in the same edit; full-width CTAs on narrow screens when appropriate |
| New modals/panels | Max-height + internal scroll; safe-area padding; keyboard-friendly spacing |
| Full-screen AI | `.fullscreen-ai` — fixed header, scrollable thread, bottom stack with safe-area |
| Grid → mobile | Collapse to 1–2 columns or horizontal scroll; never squeeze below usable tap size |

---

## Do not ship

- Desktop-only layouts with no `@media (max-width: 768px)` block for new UI
- Tap targets under 44px (e.g. 36px “Change” or icon-only buttons without padding)
- Horizontal overflow clipping text with no wrap
- Fixed elements covering content on short phone viewports
- “Will fix mobile later” — **fix mobile in the same change**

---

## When reporting completion

If the change included UI, briefly confirm responsive work (e.g. “Mobile: 2-col chip grid, 48px duration buttons, safe-area padding on section”). If the change was logic-only with no UI impact, say so explicitly.
